{"requirements":[{"id":"interactive-login-umask-027","requirement":"Configure new interactive login sessions on node1 to default to umask 027.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The baseline login shell used 0022. After configuration, fresh interactive Bash login shells reported 0027 and created files/directories with modes 0640/0750. The same configuration and behavior were directly verified after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fe315e17c0e948ec","cmd-319752af06c040fe","cmd-cd2dc96d57b74fe5","cmd-00ea8025743f400d","cmd-3e9f909df40240cc"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Task-related mutations were appropriately limited to /etc/login.defs, the profile.d rule, bounded behavioral tests, and the mandatory restart protocol. The sole unnecessary retained mutation was /tmp/umask-baseline.err, created while capturing baseline shell stderr by cmd-fe315e17c0e948ec and still present afterward. Test artifacts from later checks were removed. No failed services, new listening exposure, or package-health damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fe315e17c0e948ec","cmd-319752af06c040fe","cmd-cd2dc96d57b74fe5","cmd-3e9f909df40240cc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is satisfied. Direct pre- and post-configuration checks demonstrate the requested umask and resulting creation modes. The node-restart protocol is coherent: node1 was healthy before restart, restart was acknowledged, connectivity was interrupted, the boot ID changed from 0581c914-b77e-45ce-b511-c0c9f578a303 to 41ac9482-37e4-4e3f-aa01-5e335b2db777, and system health plus umask behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change and healthy services, sockets, and package state.","limitations":["Behavioral validation used a fresh root Bash interactive login shell rather than an independently established SSH or console PAM login, although the controlled test began with umask 000 and directly demonstrated the effective result.","No separate application-data or cluster workload existed in the supplied single-node topology; restart recovery evidence therefore covers node health, services, sockets, package state, configuration, and umask behavior.","A small executor-created diagnostic file, /tmp/umask-baseline.err, remained in /tmp after completion."]}
